Three.js r128 — MIT License
===========================

WHY THIS FILE IS HERE. MIT requires that the copyright notice and this permission
notice accompany the software. `three.min.js` sits in this directory and is
distributed by this project, so the notice has to travel with it — a licence recorded
only in a table one directory up does not accompany anything. `assets/lib/NOTICE.md`
records the claim; this file is the notice itself.

WHERE THE COPYRIGHT LINE CAME FROM. It is transcribed character for character from the
`@license` header of the vendored file itself, which is the first five lines of
`r128/three.min.js`:

    /**
     * @license
     * Copyright 2010-2021 Three.js Authors
     * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
     */

Nothing below was guessed. `tools/licence-audit.ps1` section A asserts that the exact
copyright string recorded in `NOTICE.md` appears both in `three.min.js` and in this
file, so a copyright line that drifted from the one the library actually carries — in
either direction — fails the audit.

